To compute \(\mathbf{A}^{27} + \mathbf{A}^{31} + \mathbf{A}^{40}\), we start by finding a pattern in the powers of matrix \(\mathbf{A}\). Let's denote \(\mathbf{B} = \mathbf{A}^2\).

First, calculate \(\mathbf{A}^2\):
\[
\mathbf{A}^2 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \cdot 3 + 7 \cdot (-1) & 3 \cdot 7 + 7 \cdot (-2) \\ -1 \cdot 3 + (-2) \cdot (-1) & -1 \cdot 7 + (-2) \cdot (-2) \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 9 - 7 & 21 - 14 \\ -3 + 2 & -7 + 4 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}.
\]

Next, calculate \(\mathbf{A}^3\):
\[
\mathbf{A}^3 = \mathbf{A} \cdot \mathbf{A}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 7 \\ -1 & -2 \end{pmatrix} \cdot \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 3 \cdot 2 + 7 \cdot (-1) & 3 \cdot 7 + 7 \cdot (-3) \\ -1 \cdot 2 + (-2) \cdot (-1) & -1 \cdot 7 + (-2) \cdot (-3) \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} 6 - 7 & 21 - 21 \\ -2 + 2 & -7 + 6 \end{pmatrix}
= \begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\]

We observe that \(\mathbf{A}^3 = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}\). This suggests that \(\mathbf{A}^k\) for any integer \(k\) can be expressed as:
\[
\mathbf{A}^k = \begin{cases} 
\begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix} & \text{if } k \equiv 0 \pmod{3}, \\
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix} & \text{if } k \equiv 1 \pmod{3}, \\
\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}^2 & \text{if } k \equiv 2 \pmod{3}.
\end{cases}
\]

Now, let's find \(\mathbf{A}^{27}\), \(\mathbf{A}^{31}\), and \(\mathbf{A}^{40}\):

- Since \(27 \equiv 0 \pmod{3}\), \(\mathbf{A}^{27} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix}\).
- Since \(31 \equiv 1 \pmod{3}\), \(\mathbf{A}^{31} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}\).
- Since \(40 \equiv 1 \pmod{3}\), \(\mathbf{A}^{40} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}\).

Adding these matrices together:
\[
\mathbf{A}^{27} + \mathbf{A}^{31} + \mathbf{A}^{40} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\ -1 & -3 \end{pmatrix}
